"""Preserve eight rank-five Necromancy sources for a later mechanical conference."""
import json
from prepare_spell_source_cohort import prepare, AUDIT

QUESTIONS = {
    'summon-death-knight': 'Preserve HP80,AC18 and a2d10 SHADOW GREATSWORD, Core Action/60ft/concentration up to one minute. Complete one finite summon profile: actual size,type,abilities,saves,Speed,senses,attack modifier,reach,damage type and action count. Resolve shadow as a damage/type or descriptive term explicitly, without importing an external Death Knight statblock or bonus damage. Bind legal placement, source ownership, command cost/channel, initiative, no-command behavior, summon allowance, concentration and ending under the reviewed creature lifecycle. Specify created versus supplied equipment and what remains after defeat/suppression/expiry; no recoverable80HP corpse,free greatsword,reusable donor parts or permanent recruit follows by name. Do not invent souls,planes,theology or cosmological origin; historical labels are retained only.',
    'mass-decay': 'Preserve ALL enemies in30ft taking4d8 necrotic initially, THEN2d6 per round for3ROUNDS, Core Action/range30ft/Instantaneous. Define center,geometry,enemy identification,perception/line and initial save/outcomes. Name exactly three later tick checkpoints and whether each requires an initial failed save or actual HP damage; resolve the duration contradiction explicitly. Determine shared rolls,individual persistent recipients,repeated saves/removal,suppression,death,overlapping casts and caster loss without extra ticks from entry or extra turns. The existing source damage ledger controls final HP damage; no automatic decomposition,perishable aging,disease,object destruction or new harvesting penalty is inferred from Decay. Separate initial area from later target-bound recurrence and preserve all printed dice.',
    'terror-chain': 'Preserve one target feared for3rounds and JUMPS TO NEXT IF FAILED, Core Action/60ft/3rounds. Resolve what fails,who rolls and when, the exact Frightened component/source anchor, initial/repeat save outcomes and how the chain chooses its next target. Supply finite hop count/range,timing,target uniqueness,eligible enemies/creatures,line of effect and whether each branch shares the original endpoint or receives a new bounded clock. A cyclic target list or repeated suppression must not create indefinite spread or duration. Decide how immunity,already-Frightened targets,successful saves,unavailable next targets and hard-control history where applicable affect propagation. Preserve the jump clause rather than deleting it; no unprinted damage,forced flight,telepathic target search or endless cascade.',
    'grave-gift': 'Preserve TRANSFERRING HALF HP to one ally and RESTORING THEM FULLY FROM DYING, Core Action/60ft/Instantaneous. Explicitly resolve whether half uses current HP,max HP or another stated basis,rounding,minimum payment,ability to pay and self/other target eligibility. Distinguish paid HP loss from damage,tempHP,healing and redirected effects; bind one real payment and resulting benefit so reductions or shared damage cannot refund the cost. Define fully from dying precisely against0HP,Critical state,Wounds,stability,consciousness and maximum HP; do not silently convert it either to ordinary fractional healing or full resurrection. Resolve sequence if the donor reaches0HP,dies or is protected by Death Ward, and handle dead versus dying recipients,healing prevention and failed qualification. No restoration of RP,Strain,limbs,diseases or spell slots without source authority.',
    'contagion': 'Preserve infecting a target with a DISEASE with various effects, Core Action/60ft/Instantaneous. Identify any actual supported disease profiles; if none supply a finite explicitly NEW fictional game roster with effect,save,incubation,onset,duration,progression,recovery and treatment rather than importing an outside spell or merely applying generic Poisoned. Define target eligibility,delivery and resistance/condition immunity,dispel/suppression versus actual disease persistence,diagnosis and existing cure scopes. Specify whether transmission exists at all and finite game-only contagion rules if NEW. Multiple casts must bind each disease identity and avoid unlimited stat loss or reset recovery clocks by renaming it. No real-world pathogen mechanism,source ecology,automatic epidemic or undeclared permanent penalty is inferred. Keep actual disease and curse classifications distinct.',
    'enervation': 'Preserve4d8 NECROTIC EACH ROUND and healing for HALF, Core Action/60ft/Instantaneous. Define one target or another explicit finite scope,initial event and repeated checkpoints,lifetime/concentration,attack/save/outcomes,maintenance actions and range/line requirements. Bind healing to one actual final paid HP-damage event with current rounding; distinguish tempHP,overkill,damage resistance/immunity,transfer,absorbed damage and simultaneous recipients. Identify who heals and how healing prevention/full HP or target death ends or consumes the opportunity. Compare reviewed Vampiric Touch/Lifedraw and damage sharing, without borrowing their attack or duration wholesale. No healing from nominal dice,duplicate shared/copy packets or banked missed ticks; recasts,suppression and extra turns cannot create extra rounds.',
    'negative-energy-flood': 'Preserve5d12 necrotic and CREATION OF A ZOMBIE IF A HUMANOID DIES, Core Action/60ft/Instantaneous. Define finite targets,save/outcomes and exactly which death event qualifies: this spell\'s actual resolved damage versus any later death. Use one physical corpse identity and actual humanoid eligibility through transformations;0HP alone is not necessarily death. Provide a complete bounded zombie profile or an exact reviewed source binding, creation delay,placement,controller/commands,allowance,lifetime and no-command behavior. Resolve simultaneous resurrection/Auto-Raise/other corpse claims,missing or destroyed body,already-animated remains and ending without duplicating body,equipment or material stock. Do not drop the zombie clause,import a familiar-game Undead buff or invent a new soul/afterlife relationship. Any true cosmology dependency stays deferred.',
    'danse-macabre': 'Preserve animating UP TO FIVE actual corpses as Undead, Core Action/60ft/Instantaneous. Define each eligible corpse\'s size,type,condition,completeness and prior identity, source of the resulting stats and equipment, finite duration/concentration and placement. Supply command cost,initiative/action limits,owner allowances,uncommanded behavior and independent loss/ending for five bodies under the creature lifecycle, without silently replacing the source count with one. Reconcile Wizard standard minions/Auto-Raise and Mage assets through their exact independent caps and body claims; being a caster of this spell does not grant either class feature. Preserve prior wounds,missing parts,inventory,harvest losses and origin restrictions rather than creating five refreshed resource-bearing bodies. State what happens after death,suppression or control expiry, and do not infer souls,planar access or cosmological resurrection.'
}


def main():
    coverage = json.loads((AUDIT / 'FOCUSED_SPELL_SOURCE_PREPARATION_COVERAGE.json').read_text(encoding='utf-8'))
    assert len(coverage['cohortFiles']) == 13 and coverage['distinctPreparedPendingSpellIds'] == 217
    prior = coverage['cohortFiles'] + ['ILLUSION_RANK5_SOURCE_PREPARATION.json']
    prepare(
        prefix='NECROMANCY_RANK5', title='Rank-five Necromancy source audit', questions=QUESTIONS,
        selector=lambda r: r['operational'] is None and 'Necromancy' in r['schools'] and min(v['rank'] for v in r['classAccess'].values()) == 5,
        expected_count=8, question_prefix='NE5', prior_files=prior, expected_prior_count=224,
        counterpart_ids=['spare-the-dying', 'lifedraw', 'summon-lesser-skeleton', 'cause-fear',
                         'vampiric-touch', 'death-ward', 'resurrection', 'fear'],
        pending_ids=['immolation', 'phantasmal-killer', 'mass-sleep'],
        extra_excerpts={
            'HEALING_DEATH_PLAYTEST.md': None,
            'FORM_TEMP_HP_PLAYTEST.md': None,
            'CREATURE_LIFECYCLE_PLAYTEST.md': None,
            'DAMAGE_SHARING_PLAYTEST.md': None,
            'CONTROL_STATES_PLAYTEST.md': ['Curse and disease'],
            'HEALING_PULSE_PLAYTEST.md': ['Keep the original clock', 'Targets, payments and separate budgets', 'Finite installments and independent components'],
            'CRAFTING_HARVEST_PLAYTEST.md': ['Material identity, consumption and substitution', 'Identify and harvest', 'Preservation and spoilage'],
        },
        introduction='Eight sources preserve their printed damage,80HP/AC18 summon,count-five animation,three-round recurrence and half-HP transfer. Current metadata does not supply every needed duration,statblock,command or disease procedure. Questions preserve the source promises and ask for bounded mechanical completions; no theology,afterlife or cosmological origin is reviewed. Real corpse/material identity and healing ledgers accompany the full records.',
        future_dispatch='Prepared only while Mining/shared gathering source review is active. Rebase exact dependencies before future dispatch. Preserve all source revisions and obtain source decisions before authoring cards and exact review. Cosmology remains strictly after the authorized push and verified remote commit.')


if __name__ == '__main__':
    main()
